<title>SPAIN: Spain's Popular cuts prime rate to 7.50%.</title>
<headline>Spain's Popular cuts prime rate to 7.50%.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Banco Popular said on Wednesday it was cutting its prime lending rate to 7.50 percent from 7.75 percent, effective from today.</p>
<p>This follows the 25 basis point reduction in the Bank of Spain's key money rate to 5.50 percent at Tuesday's repo auction.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
</text>
